      "writtenOn": "2022-06-16T16:47:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I realize you\u0027re just moving this and didn\u0027t write this, but `ar` is the devil and the enemy of reproducible builds (since it likes to append things). In particular see https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/295569 and the related issues. It is generally necessary to first delete any existing `ar` file before calling `ar` to not run into very unexpected behavior.\n\nAlso, in our existing gn build, we make sure not to use `ar` and use `libtool` instead (since it is quite a bit saner).",
      "revId": "b6e872974b82d7575887889994d2c67684b3e232",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
