      "writtenOn": "2022-06-16T19:10:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed, it should come from the same place.\nThe problem is that if wanted to include these frameworks through a symlink (same as we do for `usr`) Bazel would break. There are lots of existing symlinks in the Frameworks subdir in the sdk and Bazel does not handle the introduced symlink recursion well.\nAlso, grabbing the xcode path with `xcode-select` doesn\u0027t work here, as we lose the ability to run command line commands here. Kevin and I were brainstorming some other ideas for how to grab the path and thought of a couple. We\u0027ll be switching over early next week.",
      "parentUuid": "63faa553_3d664a22",
      "revId": "b6e872974b82d7575887889994d2c67684b3e232",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
